cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use K-NanoMFA in research, please cite the software and state the version, country/domain, nanomaterial, model mode, scenario date, and advanced modules used."
title: "K-NanoMFA: Country-resolved material flow analysis and environmental fate platform for nanomaterials"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Younghun
    affiliation: Kwangwoon University
    email: korea1@kw.ac.kr
version: 2.5.1
date-released: '2026-09-18'
license: MIT
abstract: "A browser-based research platform for product-informed nanomaterial inventories, optional nanoform-state accounting and dynamic nanoform-resolved environmental fate, deterministic and probabilistic static MFA, inflow- and stock-driven dynamic MFA, country and subnational domains, bundled and custom nanomaterials, trade-balanced inflow, environmental-media PECs, data reconciliation, Bayesian calibration, reduced-form multimedia fate, validation, uncertainty and sensitivity analysis, and screening life-cycle burden comparison."
keywords:
  - material flow analysis
  - product inventory
  - nano-enabled products
  - nanomaterials
  - nanoform state
  - transformation state
  - dynamic MFA
  - stock-driven MFA
  - data reconciliation
  - Bayesian calibration
  - predicted environmental concentration
  - multimedia fate
  - kinetic fate
  - dissolution
  - aggregation
  - sedimentation
  - uncertainty analysis
